# Compile-probe manifest — drives `make check-metal-compiles` for the per-arch
# kernels in this crate. Same format and same gate as the KV-codec manifest at
# crates/rmlx-kv-quant/src/metal/probes/kernels.manifest; see the README there
# for the probe layout and how to refresh a captured header snapshot.
#
# Format:  <body.metal> | <header or -> | <name:type,...> | [NAME=VALUE,...]
#   type: u = uint buffer, i = int buffer, f = float buffer, b = bfloat buffer
#
# Every kernel here takes its compile-time constants as MLX template
# arguments, so the fourth field carries representative values for them. `T`
# in the gated-delta body and `scale` in the Hadamard body are scalar 0-D
# inputs, which MLX declares as `constant int&` / `constant float&` — a numeric
# literal to the body, hence a define rather than a buffer alias.
#
# Every `.metal` file in the parent directory must appear here, as a body or as
# a `../`-prefixed header. The gate fails on one that does not.

# Dk/Dv/Hk/Hv are Qwen3.6-35B-A3B's GatedDeltaNet shape; the probe only needs
# Dk % 32 == 0 and Hv % Hk == 0 to hold.
gated_delta_step.metal | - | q:f,k:f,v:f,g:f,beta:f,state_in:f,y:f,state_out:f | Dk=128,Dv=128,Hk=16,Hv=32,T=8,InT=float,StT=float
# ROWS_PER_TILE=4 is the prefill variant; 1 is the decode variant. Only the
# larger is probed — the two differ by the value of one template int, not by
# what has to resolve.
paroquant_rotate.metal | - | x:f,packed_pairs:u,cos_theta:f,sin_theta:f,channel_scales:f,params:u,out:f | ROWS_PER_TILE=4,MAX_KROT=16,MAX_GROUP_SIZE=256,InT=float
# N and WIDTH are Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B's block and hidden size; scale is
# 1 / sqrt(N); RADIX is the radix the host dispatches with. Forward only:
# INVERSE selects where the signs apply, not what has to resolve.
signed_block_hadamard.metal | ../hadamard_header.metal | x:b,signs:f,out:b | T=bfloat,N=1024,WIDTH=5120,INVERSE=0,RADIX=16,scale=0.03125f
